#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/12
msgid ""
"Yeah, that's been the subject of debate.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，这一直有争议。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/13
msgid ""
"Whether or not it forbids any and all use of force.\n"
msgstr ""
"是否禁止一切武力使用。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/14
msgid ""
"The current constitution was originally drawn up\n"
"under the Allied occupation.\n"
msgstr ""
"现行宪法最初是在盟军占领下\n"
"制定的。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/15
msgid ""
"The first draft was even submitted by Allied GHQ.\n"
msgstr ""
"初稿甚至是盟军总司令部提交的。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/16
msgid ""
"So naturally there are some who feel the\n"
"constitution was imposed on Japan by foreigners.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以自然有人觉得，宪法是\n"
"外国人强加给日本的。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/17
msgid ""
"Things like that are never simple. Same for every\n"
"country, I guess...\n"
msgstr ""
"这种事从来都不简单。\n"
"大概每个国家都一样……\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/18
msgid ""
"One thing's for sure, though\n"
msgstr ""
"不过有一点可以肯定\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/19
msgid ""
"- not having an army let Japan focus on economic\n"
"recovery after the war.\n"
msgstr ""
"——没有军队让日本战后能专注\n"
"经济复兴。\n"

#: codec/1/158/0x9e190/20
msgid ""
"In that sense, it's the same as Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么说，和哥斯达黎加一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 473..1407
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/0
msgid ""
"Kaz, you were in the Japanese Self-Defense Force,\n"
"right?\n"
msgstr ""
"卡兹，你以前在日本自卫队待过，\n"
"对吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 1462..2117
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/1
msgid ""
"I thought that Article 9 you were talking about\n"
"earlier\n"
msgstr ""
"我之前听你说的那个第9条\n"
"来着\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 2117..2772
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/2
msgid ""
"prevented Japan from having an army...\n"
msgstr ""
"让日本不能拥有军队……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 2786..3650
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/3
msgid ""
"Yeah, and that's another subject of controversy.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，那也是个争议点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 3678..4834
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/4
msgid ""
"\"The Self-Defense Force is an organization for the\n"
"purpose of defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"“自卫队是以防卫为目的的\n"
"组织。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 4917..6199
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/5
msgid ""
"Article 9 of the constitution does not deny Japan's\n"
"right to self-defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"宪法第九条并不否认日本的\n"
"自卫权。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 6339..7202
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/6
msgid ""
"Therefore, the SDF is constitutional.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"因此，自卫队符合宪法。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 7244..7829
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/7
msgid ""
"That's Tokyo's official stance.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是东京的官方立场。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 8108..8637
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/8
msgid ""
"...Sounds complicated.\n"
msgstr ""
"……好复杂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0300_010_0
#. timeline 8637..9877
#: codec/1/158/0x9e950/9
msgid ""
"Call it what you will, it's a distinctly Japanese way\n"
"of interpreting things.\n"
msgstr ""
"不管怎么说，这都是典型的日本式\n"
"解释方式。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/0
msgid ""
"You know that today, Japan is under the American\n"
"nuclear umbrella...\n"
msgstr ""
"你知道如今日本处于美国的\n"
"核保护伞下……\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/2
msgid ""
"The U.S. vowed to retaliate against any country\n"
msgstr ""
"美国承诺会报复任何国家\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/3
msgid ""
"that launches a nuclear strike against an allied\n"
"country...\n"
msgstr ""
"那会对盟国发动核打击的\n"
"国家……\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/4
msgid ""
"That promise deters nuclear attacks against\n"
"America's allies.\n"
msgstr ""
"这一承诺威慑了对美国盟国的\n"
"核攻击。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/5
msgid ""
"Hence the term \"nuclear umbrella.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"所以叫“核保护伞”。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/6
msgid ""
"But suppose the Russians nuked Tokyo.\n"
msgstr ""
"但假设苏联用核弹打东京。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/7
msgid ""
"Would America really nuke Moscow in return?\n"
msgstr ""
"美国真会核平莫斯科作为回击？\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/8
msgid ""
"If they did, the Soviet Union would undoubtedly\n"
"retaliate.\n"
msgstr ""
"若真如此，苏联必将\n"
"报复。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/9
msgid ""
"Would Washington really be willing to risk\n"
msgstr ""
"华盛顿真愿冒险\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/10
msgid ""
"having a bomb dropped on itself in order to\n"
"avenge Japan?\n"
msgstr ""
"为向日本复仇，\n"
"不惜自己挨一颗炸弹？\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/11
msgid ""
"...I'm not so sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"…不确定。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/12
msgid ""
"Don't tell me you're still worried about Japan. After\n"
"all these years?\n"
msgstr ""
"别告诉我你还在担心日本。都\n"
"这么多年了？\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/13
msgid ""
"It's not that. I just...\n"
msgstr ""
"不是那事。我只是……\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/14
msgid ""
"To be honest, I'm not convinced, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"说实话，我也不信。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/15
msgid ""
"But Moscow faces the same dilemma. Maybe\n"
"Washington wouldn't retaliate on Japan's behalf.\n"
msgstr ""
"但莫斯科也面临同样困境。也许\n"
"华盛顿不会为日本报复。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/16
msgid ""
"Then again, maybe it would.\n"
msgstr ""
"可也许它会。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/17
msgid ""
"So you're saying Moscow wouldn't want to risk\n"
"being attacked, either...\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说莫斯科也不想冒\n"
"被攻击的风险……\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/18
msgid ""
"The whole concept of nuclear deterrence is\n"
"entirely hypothetical to begin with.\n"
msgstr ""
"核威慑这概念本身\n"
"就纯属假设。\n"

#: codec/1/159/0x9f870/19
msgid ""
"When you get down to it, it's all smoke and mirrors.\n"
msgstr ""
"说到底，全是虚张声势。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 473..1727
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/0
msgid ""
"So tell me, Kaz, how's the Self-Defense Force you\n"
"were in different from an army?\n"
msgstr ""
"那卡兹，你待过的自卫队\n"
"和军队有何不同？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 1727..2563
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/1
msgid ""
"The JSDF is set up for national defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"日本自卫队是为国防而设。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 2633..3566
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/2
msgid ""
"It's not configured for aggression against other\n"
"countries.\n"
msgstr ""
"并非为侵略他国\n"
"而配置。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 3636..4360
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/3
msgid ""
"It's what you'd call exclusive defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是所谓的专守防卫。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 4374..4834
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/4
msgid ""
"Exclusive... defense?\n"
msgstr ""
"专守……防卫？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 4834..6436
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/5
msgid ""
"It's the fundamental strategic posture of the JSDF.\n"
"No preemptive attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是自卫队的根本战略姿态。\n"
"不发动先制攻击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 6492..7648
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/6
msgid ""
"Only the minimum defensive action necessary after\n"
"an enemy attacks.\n"
msgstr ""
"只在遭敌攻击后采取\n"
"最低限度防御行动。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 7662..8400
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/7
msgid ""
"Anything defined as self defense, then.\n"
msgstr ""
"凡被界定为自卫的皆可。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 8414..9473
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/8
msgid ""
"The JSDF originated as the National Police Reserve.\n"
msgstr ""
"自卫队前身是警察预备队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 9501..11020
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/9
msgid ""
"Back then, American forces stationed in Japan\n"
"were being sent over to fight in the Korean War.\n"
msgstr ""
"当时驻日美军\n"
"被派去参加朝鲜战争。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 11117..11939
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/10
msgid ""
"So in a sense, the NPR was filling a gap.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以警预队是在补缺。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 11981..13054
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/11
msgid ""
"Police, huh... Reminds me of the Costa Rican Civil\n"
"Guard.\n"
msgstr ""
"警察啊……想起哥斯达黎加\n"
"国民警卫队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 13054..14349
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/12
msgid ""
"Yeah, exactly. They're also dispatched to provide\n"
"disaster relief.\n"
msgstr ""
"对，没错。他们也会被派去提供\n"
"灾害救援。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 14433..15130
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/13
msgid ""
"The year before I joined, they had a hell of a time\n"
msgstr ""
"我入伍前一年，他们可吃了不少苦头\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0330_000_0
#. timeline 15130..16063
#: codec/1/160/0xa04e0/14
msgid ""
"trying to rescue some buses that got hit by\n"
"landslides.\n"
msgstr ""
"去营救一些被\n"
"滑坡砸中的公交车。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/0
msgid ""
"So why'd you quit the JSDF?\n"
msgstr ""
"那你为什么退出日本自卫队？\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/1
msgid ""
"Because I didn't have a reason to be in Japan\n"
"anymore.\n"
msgstr ""
"因为我已经没有理由\n"
"继续留在日本了。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/2
msgid ""
"Reason?\n"
msgstr ""
"理由？\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/3
msgid ""
"My mom had died three years earlier, so I didn't\n"
"have to care for her anymore.\n"
msgstr ""
"我母亲三年前去世了，所以我不用\n"
"再照顾她了。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/4
msgid ""
"With her gone, there was no point hanging around\n"
"in Japan.\n"
msgstr ""
"她走了，待在日本\n"
"也没意义了。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/5
msgid ""
"Yeah, but a man with your talents could have risen\n"
"pretty high in the ranks, I imagine.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，但以你的才能，我想本可以在\n"
"军阶上爬得相当高。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/6
msgid ""
"I don't know what they made of me. Could be it\n"
"actually alienated me from the brass.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不知道他们怎么看我。可能这\n"
"反而让我和上级疏远了。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/7
msgid ""
"And personally, I could never get used to the idea\n"
"of exclusive defense.\n"
msgstr ""
"就我个人而言，始终无法接受\n"
"专守防卫这种理念。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/8
#: codec/2/905/0x389770/33
msgid ""
"Meaning?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么意思？\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/9
msgid ""
"On a strategic level,\n"
msgstr ""
"战略上讲，\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/10
msgid ""
"I can see how a country could go with the\n"
"exclusive defense model used by the JSDF,\n"
msgstr ""
"我能理解一个国家为什么会采用\n"
"自卫队那种专守防卫模式，\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/11
msgid ""
"and I've got nothing against my fellow soldiers who\n"
"believe in it.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且我对信奉这一理念的\n"
"战友们没有任何意见。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/12
msgid ""
"On a tactical level, though, it just rubbed me the\n"
"wrong way.\n"
msgstr ""
"但战术层面，这实在让我\n"
"觉得不对劲。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/13
msgid ""
"To put it simply, I was itching for a real fight.\n"
msgstr ""
"简单说，我渴望真正的战斗。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/14
msgid ""
"I figured....\n"
msgstr ""
"我想……\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/15
msgid ""
"And I felt like as long as I was in the JSDF,\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得只要还在日本自卫队，\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/16
msgid ""
"I'd never be able to stand shoulder to shoulder\n"
"with my father who was in the U.S. Army.\n"
msgstr ""
"我永远无法和我那曾在美军服役的\n"
"父亲并肩而立。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/17
msgid ""
"Seeing Yukio Mishima's suicide didn't help, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"三岛由纪夫的自杀也让我触动。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/18
msgid ""
"Yukio Mishima... the guy who wrote \"The Temple of\n"
"the Golden Pavilion\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"三岛由纪夫……就是写《金阁寺》的\n"
"那个人？\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/19
msgid ""
"The way he questioned the status quo hit home\n"
"with me.\n"
msgstr ""
"他质疑现状的方式\n"
"让我深有共鸣。\n"

#: codec/1/160/0xa0a60/20
msgid ""
"Not that I admired his vision or anything. But it did\n"
"get me thinking, that's for sure.\n"
msgstr ""
"倒不是钦佩他的愿景。但这确实\n"
"让我思考很多，毫无疑问。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 445..1198
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/0
msgid ""
"Don't forget to give the MSF staff assignments.\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了给MSF员工分配任务。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 1267..2173
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/1
msgid ""
"Where you place people will determine how Mother\n"
"Base grows..\n"
msgstr ""
"人员配置决定Mother\n"
"Base的发展。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 2396..3357
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/3
msgid ""
"That goes for me, too. Assign me wherever you\n"
"think is best.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也一样。把我派到\n"
"你觉得最合适的地方。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 3371..4193
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/4
msgid ""
"You? I thought you were second-in-command.\n"
msgstr ""
"你？你不是二把手吗。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4207..4667
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/5
msgid ""
"Don't worry, I've got that covered.\n"
msgstr ""
"放心，那事我来管。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4667..6018
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/6
msgid ""
"But MSF is still small, and I don't have the leisure\n"
"of sitting around on my butt all day.\n"
msgstr ""
"但MSF还小，我可没空\n"
"整天闲坐着。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 6673..7244
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/7
msgid ""
"I see your point, but...\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂，可是……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 7258..8442
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/8
msgid ""
"Not to brag or anything, but I'd kick ass at\n"
"whatever job you gave me.\n"
msgstr ""
"不是吹牛，你派我干啥\n"
"我都能干得漂亮。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8456..9445
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/9
msgid ""
"Put me in the area you want to focus on\n"
"developing most.\n"
msgstr ""
"把我放到你最想重点\n"
"发展的领域。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 9473..10267
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/10
msgid ""
"I'll take real good care of the staff there.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会好好照顾那里的员工。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 10267..10699
#: codec/1/161/0xa11f0/11
msgid ""
"Easy, Kaz.\n"
msgstr ""
"别急，卡兹。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 445..1156
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/0
msgid ""
"You've probably heard this a million times, Snake,\n"
msgstr ""
"这话你可能听过无数遍了，SNAKE，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 1170..2117
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/1
msgid ""
"but you should always avoid combat with the\n"
"enemy when possible.\n"
msgstr ""
"但只要能避免，就尽量别和\n"
"敌人交战。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 2382..3218
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/3
msgid ""
"We're outnumbered and in unfamiliar territory.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们人少，又在陌生地带。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 3232..4416
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/4
msgid ""
"We won't survive long in a straight fight, even with\n"
"you on our side.\n"
msgstr ""
"正面硬拼撑不了多久，就算\n"
"有你在也一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 4444..5781
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/5
msgid ""
"I know. Avoiding combat is rule number one in a\n"
"sneaking mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。潜入任务第一条\n"
"就是避免交战。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 5795..7174
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/6
msgid ""
"That's right. Don't let the enemy know where you\n"
"are, and attack only when necessary,\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。别让敌人发现你的\n"
"位置，只在必要时出手，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 7174..7955
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/7
msgid ""
"using hit-and-run tactics to cripple them...\n"
msgstr ""
"用打了就跑的战术削弱他们……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0010_000_0
#. timeline 8010..8693
#: codec/1/164/0xa47a0/8
msgid ""
"It's the essence of guerrilla warfare.\n"
msgstr ""
"这就是游击战的精髓。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 459..919
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/0
msgid ""
"Can I ask you a favor, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"能拜托你件事吗，SNAKE？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 919..1657
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/1
msgid ""
"If you ask nicely.\n"
msgstr ""
"你好好求我就行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 1657..2605
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/2
msgid ""
"To make MSF bigger, we need to do some\n"
"recruiting.\n"
msgstr ""
"要壮大MSF，就得\n"
"招些人手。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 2605..3371
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/3
msgid ""
"Yeah... What's your point?\n"
msgstr ""
"嗯……你想说啥？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 3371..5224
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/4
msgid ""
"I want you to avoid killing enemy soldiers as much\n"
"as possible and send them back using Fulton\n"
"recovery.\n"
msgstr ""
"我希望你尽量避免杀死敌方士兵\n"
"尽可能用富尔顿回收\n"
"把他们送回来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 5224..6032
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/5
msgid ""
"Not much we can do with a corpse except give it a\n"
"funeral.\n"
msgstr ""
"尸体除了下葬\n"
"也没别的用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 6032..6352
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_myo_rad_0120_000_0
#. timeline 4750..5140
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/6
#: codec/2/917/0x395bd0/6
msgid ""
"Obviously.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 6366..7272
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/7
msgid ""
"Put 'em to sleep, knock 'em out...hold 'em up, even.\n"
msgstr ""
"打晕、弄睡……甚至逼降都行。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 7272..8526
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/8
msgid ""
"And if you do have to fight, try to leave them near\n"
"death instead of dead.\n"
msgstr ""
"真要打，尽量让他们濒死\n"
"而不是死亡。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 8540..9849
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/9
msgid ""
"And then use the Fulton recovery system...sounds\n"
"easy enough.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后用富尔顿回收系统……听着\n"
"挺简单。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0650_000_0
#. timeline 9863..11772
#: codec/1/164/0xa4b00/10
msgid ""
"You know what'd be really nice, though. If we had a\n"
"way to Fulton recover anybody at anytime...\n"
msgstr ""
"不过要是能随时\n"
"富尔顿回收任何人就好了……\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/0
msgid ""
"Don't carry any more gear than you need.\n"
msgstr ""
"别带多余的装备。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/1
msgid ""
"If you try and stuff your entire arsenal into your\n"
"backpack,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果你试图把你的全部武器都塞进\n"
"背包里，\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/2
msgid ""
"it'll be too heavy and your mobility will be impaired.\n"
msgstr ""
"太重会拖慢你的行动。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/3
msgid ""
"You'll only be hurting yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"吃亏的是你自己。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/4
msgid ""
"I know. Take only what you need. Every rookie\n"
"knows that.\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道。只带需要的。新兵\n"
"都懂。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/5
msgid ""
"You can check the weight of your gear before\n"
"heading out.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可以在出发前检查\n"
"装备的重量。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5290/6
msgid ""
"So make sure you do.\n"
msgstr ""
"记得查一下。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 445..1476
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/0
msgid ""
"Even a born warrior like you gets hand tremors,\n"
"Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"就算你这种天生战士也会手抖，\n"
"Snake。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 1518..2229
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/1
msgid ""
"It happens even when you're full of stamina,\n"
msgstr ""
"体力满时也会抖，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 2229..3747
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/2
msgid ""
"and it only gets worse when you're tired -\n"
"especially with larger, heavier weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"累了只会更糟，\n"
"尤其拿更大更重的武器时。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 3775..4890
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/3
msgid ""
"Obviously, you'll get better aim crouching than you\n"
"will standing.\n"
msgstr ""
"显然，蹲下时你的瞄准会比\n"
"站立时更好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 4904..5976
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/4
msgid ""
"And when you use a scope, setting your sights on\n"
"a single point\n"
msgstr ""
"而当你使用瞄准镜时，将准星对准\n"
"一个点\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 5976..6840
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/5
msgid ""
"will gradually give you a more precise aim.\n"
msgstr ""
"瞄准会逐渐更精准。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 6924..7732
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/6
msgid ""
"As we develop better weapons at Mother Base,\n"
"though,\n"
msgstr ""
"母基地造出好武器后，\n"
"不过，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 7732..8986
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/7
msgid ""
"you may gain access to new, low-tremor versions\n"
"of the same guns.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可能会获得同一批枪械的新的、低抖动\n"
"版本。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 9000..9710
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/8
msgid ""
"So if you expect the shakes to be a problem,\n"
msgstr ""
"要是担心手抖，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 9752..10574
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/9
msgid ""
"you might want to put some resources into R&D.\n"
msgstr ""
"不妨投点资源搞研发。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 10574..11744
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/10
msgid ""
"I'll keep it in mind. Then again, the more you use a\n"
"weapon,\n"
msgstr ""
"记下了。话说你越用一件\n"
"武器，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 11744..12301
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/11
msgid ""
"the more your hands get used to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"手就越习惯。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0050_000_0
#. timeline 12301..13193
#: codec/1/165/0xa5540/12
msgid ""
"Sometimes it pays to be faithful to your gun.\n"
msgstr ""
"忠于自己的枪有时也有好处。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5a00/0
msgid ""
"Choosing the right uniform is crucial.\n"
msgstr ""
"选对制服很关键。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5a00/1
msgid ""
"Pick one that matches the mission objective and\n"
"your own combat style.\n"
msgstr ""
"挑一个既符合任务目标、\n"
"又契合你战斗风格的吧。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/0
msgid ""
"Jungle fatigues are made for jungle combat.\n"
msgstr ""
"丛林迷彩就是为丛林战设计的。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/1
msgid ""
"They provide decent protection and let you carry\n"
"a fair number of weapons. Your standard uniform,\n"
"basically.\n"
msgstr ""
"防护不错，还能带\n"
"不少武器。基本就是你的\n"
"标准制服。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/2
msgid ""
"The distinguishing factor is that your camo index\n"
"will vary - a lot - depending on the area.\n"
msgstr ""
"区别在于，你的迷彩指数\n"
"会因区域不同而大幅变化。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/3
msgid ""
"Wear a pattern that makes you blend in with your\n"
"surroundings and your camo index goes up.\n"
msgstr ""
"穿上能让你融入周围环境的\n"
"迷彩，你的迷彩指数就会上升。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/4
msgid ""
"Wear something that clashes and you'll stick out\n"
"like a sore thumb.\n"
msgstr ""
"穿得格格不入，你就会\n"
"特别显眼。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5b10/5
msgid ""
"Pick the right pattern for the occasion - Sigint\n"
"used to lecture me on it all the time.\n"
msgstr ""
"根据场合选对迷彩——Sigint\n"
"以前老是跟我念叨这个。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/0
msgid ""
"The sneaking suit is a specialized uniform for\n"
"stealth missions.\n"
msgstr ""
"潜行服是专为\n"
"潜行任务设计的特殊制服。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/1
msgid ""
"It provides excellent camo in any stage.\n"
msgstr ""
"任何地形都能提供极佳迷彩。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/2
msgid ""
"Even better, you won't make a sound when you\n"
"walk.\n"
msgstr ""
"更妙的是，走路时\n"
"不会出声。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/3
msgid ""
"So I won't need to tiptoe all the time.\n"
msgstr ""
"那我就不用一直踮着脚了。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/4
msgid ""
"And, to top it off, it also makes your wounds heal\n"
"faster.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且它还能让伤口\n"
"好得更快。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/5
msgid ""
"The fabric exerts just the right amount of\n"
"pressure on your body to help stop bleeding.\n"
msgstr ""
"这种面料会对你的身体施加恰到好处的\n"
"压力，帮助止血。\n"

#: codec/1/165/0xa5e20/6
msgid ""
"Not a bad little trick.\n"
msgstr ""
"这招不错。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/0
msgid ""
"The battle dress uniform is the opposite of the\n"
"sneaking suit\n"
msgstr ""
"战斗服与潜行服\n"
"正好相反\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/1
msgid ""
"in that it's specialized for combat.\n"
msgstr ""
"它是专为战斗设计的。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/2
msgid ""
"It lets you carry plenty of weapons and ammo, and\n"
"provides excellent protection.\n"
msgstr ""
"它能让你携带大量武器和弹药，并\n"
"提供出色的防护。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/3
msgid ""
"Not the best choice for sneaking, but if you feel\n"
"like playing one-man army,\n"
msgstr ""
"虽然不适合潜行，但如果你想\n"
"玩一人成军的话，\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/4
msgid ""
"this is the uniform of choice.\n"
msgstr ""
"就选它。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/5
msgid ""
"Looks pretty damn heavy.\n"
msgstr ""
"看着真够沉的。\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/6
msgid ""
"It is. You won't be able to move as fast with it on,\n"
msgstr ""
"确实。穿上它移动会变慢，\n"

#: codec/1/166/0xa60d0/7
msgid ""
"meaning it's not good for running away, either.\n"
"Keep that in mind.\n"
msgstr ""
"也就是说它也不适合逃跑。\n"
"记住这一点。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 459..1462
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/0
msgid ""
"Naked... That's exactly what you are with this\n"
"uniform.\n"
msgstr ""
"裸装……穿这套，\n"
"你就跟没穿一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 1476..2187
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/1
msgid ""
"The pants are the same as the jungle fatigues.\n"
msgstr ""
"裤子跟丛林迷彩一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 2201..3009
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/2
msgid ""
"Obviously, since you're exposing your bare skin,\n"
msgstr ""
"毕竟皮肤都露在外面，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 3009..3859
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/3
msgid ""
"your defense and camo index are going to be low.\n"
msgstr ""
"防御和迷彩指数都会降低。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 3928..5001
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/4
msgid ""
"On the plus side, it's so light you can move around\n"
"quicker.\n"
msgstr ""
"好处是够轻，移动\n"
"更快。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 5335..6102
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/5
msgid ""
"Good for showing off muscles, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"也适合秀肌肉。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 6130..6896
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/6
msgid ""
"Hey, Snake. I heard they gave you your old code\n"
"name\n"
msgstr ""
"嘿，SNAKE。听说他们给了你\n"
"旧代号\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 6896..7718
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/7
msgid ""
"because you used to run around with your shirt\n"
"off. Is that true?\n"
msgstr ""
"因为你以前总光着膀子\n"
"到处跑。真的吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 7718..8526
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/8
msgid ""
"Don't believe everything you hear. They called me\n"
"\"Naked\"\n"
msgstr ""
"别什么都信。他们叫我\n"
"“裸蛇”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 8526..9919
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/9
msgid ""
"because I went in without gear or food. I had to\n"
"procure everything on site...\n"
msgstr ""
"是因为我不带装备和食物潜入。一切\n"
"都得就地筹措……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 9933..10964
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/10
msgid ""
"You mean they sent you into the jungle without\n"
"even a pair of pants?!\n"
msgstr ""
"你是说他们连条裤子都不给你\n"
"就把你扔进丛林？！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 11020..12483
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/11
msgid ""
"On a HALO jump from 35,000 feet?! Sweet Jesus,\n"
"you are a legend!!\n"
msgstr ""
"三万五千英尺\n"
"HALO跳伞？！天，你真是传奇！！\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 12483..13207
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/12
msgid ""
"...You're busting my balls, aren't you, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""
"……你在耍我吧，卡兹？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 13249..13653
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/13
msgid ""
"A little bit, yeah.\n"
msgstr ""
"有点，没错。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0040_040_0
#. timeline 13667..14099
#: codec/1/166/0xa63e0/14
msgid ""
"...Hilarious\n"
msgstr ""
"……真好笑\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 445..1393
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/0
msgid ""
"COoperative OPerationS, or CO-OPS for short,\n"
msgstr ""
"COoperative OPerationS，简称CO-OPS，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 1421..2452
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/1
msgid ""
"is the term for taking on missions in teams of two\n"
"or more.\n"
msgstr ""
"指以两人以上小队\n"
"执行任务。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 2479..3260
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/2
msgid ""
"The basic CO-OPS unit is a two-man cell.\n"
msgstr ""
"CO-OPS的基本单位是双人小组。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 3287..4304
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/3
msgid ""
"Even a single teammate is great to have in enemy\n"
"territory.\n"
msgstr ""
"在敌占区哪怕只有一个队友\n"
"也强得多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 4318..5308
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/4
msgid ""
"And there are actually quite a few things you can't\n"
"do by yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且有些事一个人\n"
"还真做不了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 5335..6311
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/5
msgid ""
"You can help each other climb walls, divide up\n"
"mission roles...\n"
msgstr ""
"可以互相帮忙爬墙、\n"
"分工执行任务……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 6394..7634
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/6
msgid ""
"On the other hand, if one of you is spotted, the\n"
"other one's screwed, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"但反过来说，一人被发现，\n"
"另一个也完了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 7648..8665
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/7
msgid ""
"And it's kind of tough for two people to hide in one\n"
"small space.\n"
msgstr ""
"而且两个人挤一个小地方\n"
"挺难的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 8679..9626
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/8
msgid ""
"Good point. But what's more important than\n"
"anything\n"
msgstr ""
"说得好。但比\n"
"什么都\n"
"更重要"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 9626..10309
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/9
msgid ""
"is how close you are to your comrades.\n"
msgstr ""
"是你和同伴的默契。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 10309..11674
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/10
msgid ""
"Well said. Working as a two-man cell can make the\n"
"mission easier or harder\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。双人小组能让任务\n"
"变简单还是变难\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 11674..12357
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/11
msgid ""
"depending on how well you work together.\n"
msgstr ""
"全看你们配合得如何。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 12427..13569
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/12
msgid ""
"It's also good to note that if you've got a clear,\n"
"specific objective,\n"
msgstr ""
"还有，如果你有清晰、\n"
"具体的目标，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 13583..14558
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/13
msgid ""
"it can be to your advantage to use an even bigger\n"
"team.\n"
msgstr ""
"使用更大的\n"
"队伍可能对你有利。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 14600..16021
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/14
msgid ""
"That said, teams of three or more run a much\n"
"greater risk of being spotted.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过三人以上的队伍被发现的\n"
"风险会大得多。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 16035..17303
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/15
msgid ""
"Yeah. In a sneaking mission, the fewer people you\n"
"have,\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊。在潜行任务中，人越少\n"
"越好，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0060_000_0
#. timeline 17303..17902
#: codec/1/166/0xa6910/16
msgid ""
"the easier it is to get around.\n"
msgstr ""
"行动越方便。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 445..1866
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/0
msgid ""
"Another thing - during a mission you can assume\n"
"what we'll call the Snake Formation.\n"
msgstr ""
"还有一点——任务中可以组成\n"
"所谓的SNAKE阵形。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 1894..2995
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/1
msgid ""
"Same as your code name - but probably not\n"
"standard operating procedure\n"
msgstr ""
"和代号一样，但对\n"
"单打独斗的人\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 2995..3845
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/2
msgid ""
"for a guy who specializes in going solo.\n"
msgstr ""
"大概不算标准战术。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 3845..4904
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/3
msgid ""
"Damn right. There's only room for one Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。SNAKE只能有一个。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 4931..5851
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/4
msgid ""
"In CO-OPS, though, it's a highly effective formation.\n"
msgstr ""
"合作任务里，这阵形很有效。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 5851..6979
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/5
msgid ""
"The signal for Snake Formation is to tap your\n"
"teammate on the shoulder.\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE阵形的信号是拍一下\n"
"队友的肩膀。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 7244..8512
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/6
msgid ""
"Can't form up until you're close enough to reach\n"
"out and touch someone.\n"
msgstr ""
"得靠近到能伸手碰到人\n"
"才能组队。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 8526..9501
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/7
msgid ""
"Entering Snake Formation is called going \"Snake In.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"进入SNAKE阵形叫“Snake In”。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 9529..10755
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/8
msgid ""
"When you're Snake In, the soldier at the front of\n"
"the line controls movement.\n"
msgstr ""
"Snake In时，队首的士兵\n"
"负责控制移动。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0080_000_0
#. timeline 10797..11842
#: codec/1/167/0xa7370/9
msgid ""
"The soldiers in back focus on scouting and attack.\n"
msgstr ""
"后面的士兵专注侦察和攻击。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 445..1448
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/0
msgid ""
"Just because your heart stops doesn't mean you're\n"
"dead immediately.\n"
msgstr ""
"心脏停止跳动并不意味着你会\n"
"立刻死亡。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 1476..2521
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/1
msgid ""
"Right. The heart just circulates blood through the\n"
"body.\n"
msgstr ""
"对。心脏只是负责让血液\n"
"在体内循环。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 2549..4221
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/2
msgid ""
"But stopping it does cut oxygen supply to the\n"
"brain - you'll be dead soon after.\n"
msgstr ""
"但停跳会切断大脑的氧气供应——\n"
"很快就会死。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4249..4862
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/3
msgid ""
"Which is why we have CPR.\n"
msgstr ""
"所以要心肺复苏。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 4904..5419
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/4
msgid ""
"Let's say your heart does stop.\n"
msgstr ""
"假设你的心脏停跳了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 5419..6770
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/5
msgid ""
"If someone performs CPR before your brain cells\n"
"die you can recover.\n"
msgstr ""
"脑细胞死前有人做心肺复苏，\n"
"你就能恢复。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 6826..7871
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/6
msgid ""
"In CO-OPS, when the LIFE Gauge drops to zero,\n"
msgstr ""
"合作任务中，生命值降到零时，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 7871..8498
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/7
msgid ""
"it means you're in a near-death state.\n"
msgstr ""
"意味着你处于濒死状态。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 8498..9250
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/8
msgid ""
"You won't be able to move or anything else.\n"
msgstr ""
"你将无法移动或做任何事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 9264..10574
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/9
msgid ""
"Performing CPR on near-death teammates can\n"
"bring them back into action.\n"
msgstr ""
"对濒死的队友做心肺复苏\n"
"能让他们重返战斗。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 10616..11828
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/10
msgid ""
"Of course, performing CPR in the middle of battle\n"
"isn't exactly safe.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，在战斗中做心肺复苏\n"
"并不安全。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 11842..12427
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/11
msgid ""
"You're leaving yourself exposed.\n"
msgstr ""
"你把自己暴露了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 12455..13820
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/12
msgid ""
"Even so, in CO-OPS you and your teammates are\n"
"all in the same boat.\n"
msgstr ""
"但合作任务里你和队友\n"
"同舟共济。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 13820..14684
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/13
msgid ""
"Don't think you can get away with leaving one of\n"
"them behind.\n"
msgstr ""
"别以为丢下他们中的谁\n"
"能没事。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 14712..16035
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/14
msgid ""
"I wouldn't think of it. And I'd expect them to do the\n"
"same for me.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不会那么想。我也指望他们\n"
"同样对我。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 16049..16927
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/15
msgid ""
"If you let all your teammates die during a mission,\n"
msgstr ""
"如果任务中你让所有队友都死了，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 16955..17540
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/16
msgid ""
"there'll be nobody left to save you.\n"
msgstr ""
"就没人能来救你了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0090_000_0
#. timeline 17540..18320
#: codec/1/167/0xa7780/17
msgid ""
"And then it's game over.\n"
msgstr ""
"然后就结束了。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/0
msgid ""
"Stand still when you're Snake In and you and your\n"
"teammates will start to get in sync.\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE IN时站住不动，你和队友\n"
"就会开始同步。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/1
msgid ""
"In sync?\n"
msgstr ""
"同步？\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/2
msgid ""
"That's right. Stay still together and you'll enter\n"
"Snake Sync mode.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。一起站住不动，就会进入\n"
"SNAKE同步模式。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/3
msgid ""
"The synergy will give you a boost in performance.\n"
msgstr ""
"协同效应会提升你的表现。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/4
msgid ""
"You'll move faster, recover faster, and have better\n"
"camouflage.\n"
msgstr ""
"移动更快，恢复更快，伪装\n"
"也更好。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/5
msgid ""
"In other words, we're at our best when we're in the\n"
"same groove.\n"
msgstr ""
"就是说，步调一致时\n"
"我们最强。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/6
msgid ""
"You got it. If you've got a big task ahead,\n"
msgstr ""
"明白了。如果前面有艰巨任务，\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/7
msgid ""
"it can't hurt to take some time to get in sync.\n"
msgstr ""
"花点时间同步没坏处。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/8
msgid ""
"Like I said before, the benefits you get from Snake\n"
"Sync\n"
msgstr ""
"就像我之前说的，你从Snake\n"
"Sync获得的好处\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/9
msgid ""
"depend on your camaraderie.\n"
msgstr ""
"取决于战友情。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/10
msgid ""
"I hear ya.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/11
msgid ""
"It's a lot easier knowing you've got someone you\n"
"know and trust covering your back.\n"
msgstr ""
"知道有信得过的人替你掩护，\n"
"会轻松很多。\n"

#: codec/1/168/0xa84e0/12
msgid ""
"It lets you focus that much more on what you have\n"
"to do.\n"
msgstr ""
"它能让你更加专注于你必须\n"
"要做的事情。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 445..1407
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/0
msgid ""
"If camaraderie represents how much your\n"
"teammates trust you,\n"
msgstr ""
"战友情谊代表\n"
"队友对你的信任，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 1421..2298
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/1
msgid ""
"then heroism shows how high your reputation is.\n"
msgstr ""
"那英雄度就代表你的声望有多高。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 2312..2688
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/2
msgid ""
"\"Heroism?\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“英雄度？”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 2702..3246
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/3
msgid ""
"That's right, heroism.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错，英雄度。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 3274..4583
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/4
msgid ""
"Your reputation affects your ability to recruit new\n"
"members to MSF.\n"
msgstr ""
"你的声望影响你招募新成员\n"
"加入MSF的能力。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 4611..5948
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/5
msgid ""
"With higher heroism, it won't take as long to\n"
"convince guys to join our cause\n"
msgstr ""
"英雄度越高，说服别人加入\n"
"就越快\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 5948..6673
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/6
msgid ""
"and send 'em back by Fulton recovery.\n"
msgstr ""
"再用富尔顿回收送回来。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 6854..7857
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/7
msgid ""
"So how do I get this \"heroism\" thing to go up?\n"
msgstr ""
"那怎么提升这个“英雄度”？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 7871..9292
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/8
msgid ""
"Lots of ways. Complete tough missions. Avoid\n"
"unnecessary bloodshed...\n"
msgstr ""
"方法很多。完成高难任务。避免\n"
"无谓杀戮……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 9292..10685
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/9
msgid ""
"And don't get caught by the enemy like a deer in\n"
"headlights, or you'll never be heroic.\n"
msgstr ""
"别像被车灯照到的鹿一样被敌人抓住，\n"
"否则永远当不了英雄。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 10699..11647
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/10
msgid ""
"Also, getting out there and attacking the enemy in\n"
"CO-OPS\n"
msgstr ""
"还有，主动出击，在\n"
"合作模式中打敌人\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 11647..12455
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/11
msgid ""
"will boost your reputation among your teammates.\n"
msgstr ""
"能提升你在队友中的声望。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 12483..13444
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/12
msgid ""
"Of course, it'll get the enemy gunning right for you,\n"
"too.\n"
msgstr ""
"当然，这也会让敌人把枪口\n"
"对准你。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 13500..14140
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/13
msgid ""
"But don't sweat it. Be yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"别紧张。做你自己。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 14154..15520
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/14
msgid ""
"Be the Boss. From where I'm standing, you're\n"
"plenty heroic already.\n"
msgstr ""
"做BOSS。在我看来，你已经\n"
"够英雄了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0110_000_0
#. timeline 15520..15938
#: codec/1/168/0xa8980/15
msgid ""
"Knock it off.\n"
msgstr ""
"少来。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/0
msgid ""
"In CO-OPS, maintaining close communications with\n"
"your teammates is crucial.\n"
msgstr ""
"合作任务中，与队友保持紧密通讯\n"
"至关重要。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/1
msgid ""
"Absolutely. Losing track of each other on the\n"
"battlefield is a good way\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。在战场上失去彼此的踪迹\n"
"是个好办法\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/2
msgid ""
"for a unit to get itself wiped out.\n"
msgstr ""
"整支部队就会被全灭。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/3
msgid ""
"Enemy positions. Orders. Distress calls.\n"
msgstr ""
"敌情。命令。求救。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/4
msgid ""
"When communications break down, you get picked\n"
"off one by one.\n"
msgstr ""
"当通讯中断时，你会被\n"
"逐个击破。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/5
msgid ""
"Now, about CO-OPS Comms.\n"
msgstr ""
"说说合作通讯。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/6
msgid ""
"CO-OPS Comms…\n"
msgstr ""
"合作通讯……\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/7
msgid ""
"It's a radio system for communicating with CO-OPS\n"
"teammates.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是与合作模式\n"
"队友通讯的无线电。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/8
msgid ""
"First open the menu, then select \"CO-OPS Comms.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"先打开菜单，选择“合作通讯”。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/9
msgid ""
"After that, press one button to choose a category,\n"
msgstr ""
"然后按一个键选类别，\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/10
msgid ""
"then another button to select the actual message.\n"
msgstr ""
"再按另一个键选具体讯息。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/11
msgid ""
"So basically you use different combinations of two\n"
"buttons\n"
msgstr ""
"所以基本上，你使用两个按键的\n"
"不同组合\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/12
msgid ""
"to send different messages.\n"
msgstr ""
"发送不同讯息。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/13
msgid ""
"Easy enough.\n"
msgstr ""
"简单。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/14
msgid ""
"You can set which messages go with which\n"
"buttons during mission prep.\n"
msgstr ""
"任务准备时可设定各按键对应的\n"
"讯息。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/15
msgid ""
"Sounds like it's going to be a pain to send\n"
"messages until I get used to it.\n"
msgstr ""
"感觉在习惯之前发送讯息\n"
"会很麻烦。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/16
msgid ""
"Then why don't you assign CO-OPS Comms to\n"
"whatever button you like?\n"
msgstr ""
"那不如把合作任务通讯设到\n"
"你喜欢的按键上？\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/17
msgid ""
"That should make things a little quicker and easier.\n"
msgstr ""
"这样应该会更快更轻松。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/18
msgid ""
"Just go to \"Key Config\".\n"
msgstr ""
"进\"按键配置\"。\n"

#: codec/1/169/0xa9240/19
msgid ""
"I'll give it a try.\n"
msgstr ""
"我试试看。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 473..1588
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/0
msgid ""
"Snake, you familiar with the Japanese word\n"
"\"kotodama\"?\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，你听过日本的\n"
"\"言灵\"这个词吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 1880..2368
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/1
msgid ""
"Kotodama...?\n"
msgstr ""
"言灵？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 2382..3329
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/2
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, there's no direct equivalent in\n"
"English...\n"
msgstr ""
"很遗憾，英文里没有直接对应的\n"
"说法……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 3329..4458
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/3
msgid ""
"But to keep it simple, let's call it a sort of \"Battle\n"
"Cry.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"但简单来说，我们就叫它一种“战\n"
"吼”吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 4527..5029
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/4
msgid ""
"\"Battle Cry,\" huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"\"战吼\"啊。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 5071..6436
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/5
msgid ""
"Right. But, Kotodama is actually a deep Japanese\n"
"concept.\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。但言灵其实是日本很深的\n"
"概念。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 6561..7565
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/6
msgid ""
"\"Koto\" means word, and \"dama\" means spirit.\n"
msgstr ""
"\"言\"是词语，\"灵\"是灵魂。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 7578..8791
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/7
msgid ""
"It signifies that words have power that affect our\n"
"reality...\n"
msgstr ""
"它意味着言语拥有影响我们\n"
"现实的力量……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 9306..10128
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/8
msgid ""
"Ah... You feeling OK?\n"
msgstr ""
"呃……你没事吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 10128..11103
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/9
msgid ""
"Guess I made it sound kind of like mumbo-jumbo,\n"
"huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"看来我说得有点像迷信了，\n"
"是吧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 11229..12580
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/10
msgid ""
"Seriously, though, haven't you ever felt energized\n"
"when a teammate cheered you on?\n"
msgstr ""
"不过说真的，队友为你加油时\n"
"你没觉得浑身是劲吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 12580..14168
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/11
msgid ""
"Or - the other way around - ever had your legs cut\n"
"out from under you by a thoughtless remark?\n"
msgstr ""
"反过来，一句无心之言\n"
"也可能让你泄气。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 14349..15645
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/12
msgid ""
"I know the feeling. Words can have a powerful\n"
"mental effect on people.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂。话语能对人的心理\n"
"产生巨大影响。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 15659..16272
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/13
msgid ""
"Same goes for CO-OPS Comms.\n"
msgstr ""
"合作通讯也一样。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 16300..17359
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/14
msgid ""
"Offering praise to somebody could make them run\n"
"faster than usual.\n"
msgstr ""
"对某人给予赞扬可能会让他们跑得\n"
"比平时更快。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 17373..18822
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/15
msgid ""
"Or make somebody who thinks they're done for get\n"
"up and fight again... See what I'm saying?\n"
msgstr ""
"也能让以为没救的人重新站起来战斗……\n"
"明白吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 18822..19825
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/16
msgid ""
"I get the picture. So it works in reverse, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"我懂了。所以反过来也成立。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0130_010_1
#. timeline 19853..21329
#: codec/1/169/0xa98c0/17
msgid ""
"The powers of words are many and varied. Try\n"
"using them for yourself.\n"
msgstr ""
"话语的力量多种多样。你自己\n"
"也试试看吧。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/0
msgid ""
"Up to two people can fit inside a cardboard box.\n"
msgstr ""
"纸箱里最多能装两个人。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/1
msgid ""
"Tell me how!\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么弄！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/2
msgid ""
"Move close to a box with a teammate inside and\n"
"an Icon will appear.\n"
msgstr ""
"靠近有队友的纸箱时，\n"
"会出现图标。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/3
msgid ""
"Then press <I=ACT>.\n"
msgstr ""
"再按<I=ACT>。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/4
msgid ""
"You'll stay inside as long as <I=ACT> is pressed.\n"
msgstr ""
"按住<I=ACT>就能一直待在里面。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/5
msgid ""
"So... Same as Snake Formation, huh.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟SNAKE阵型一样啊。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/6
msgid ""
"Exactly the same. In fact, when you put on a\n"
"cardboard box when Snake In,\n"
msgstr ""
"完全一样。实际上，当Snake In穿上\n"
"纸箱时，\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/7
msgid ""
"both of you can climb inside.\n"
msgstr ""
"两人都能钻进去。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/8
msgid ""
"A box big enough to hold me and my buddy...\n"
msgstr ""
"能装下我和队友的大纸箱……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/9
msgid ""
"These are fine times we live in, eh, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""
"真是个好时代啊，卡兹？\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaa690/10
msgid ""
"Yyyyeah, sure, Boss...\n"
msgstr ""
"是……是啊，BOSS……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/0
msgid ""
"Snake, the R&D team came up with something new...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，研发组搞出了新东西……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/1
msgid ""
"What is this?!\n"
msgstr ""
"这啥？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/2
msgid ""
"It's a cardboard tank. It's got enough room for two\n"
"people,\n"
msgstr ""
"这是一辆纸板坦克。它足够容纳两\n"
"个人，\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/3
msgid ""
"same as any other cardboard box.\n"
msgstr ""
"跟普通纸箱一样。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/4
msgid ""
"Apparently the guy in front drives, and the guy in\n"
"back is the gunner...\n"
msgstr ""
"据说前面的人负责驾驶，后面的人\n"
"是炮手……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/5
msgid ""
"Hold on. Kaz, who the hell came up this thing?!\n"
msgstr ""
"等等。卡兹，谁搞出这玩意的？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/6
msgid ""
"I'm sorry, Boss. He meant well, I swear.\n"
msgstr ""
"抱歉，BOSS。他真是好意。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/7
msgid ""
"I know it's nowhere near as good as a real tank,\n"
"but still...\n"
msgstr ""
"我知道它远不如真正的坦克，\n"
"但还是……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/8
msgid ""
"It's BRILLIANT!!\n"
msgstr ""
"太棒了！！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/9
#: codec/1/195/0xc38b0/10
#: codec/1/240/0xf0320/28
msgid ""
"Huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"啊？\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/10
msgid ""
"The perfect synthesis of stealth and attack power.\n"
msgstr ""
"隐匿与攻击力的完美结合。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/11
msgid ""
"Compact, elegant design. The finest example of a\n"
"weapon I've ever seen!\n"
msgstr ""
"紧凑、优雅的设计。这是我见过\n"
"最精良的武器典范！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/12
msgid ""
"Seriously, Kaz, I need to meet the guy who made\n"
"this. I wanna shake his hand.\n"
msgstr ""
"说真的，Kaz，我得见见做这个的\n"
"人。我想跟他握个手。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/13
msgid ""
"Y-you're serious? Snake, look at it, it's...\n"
msgstr ""
"你、当真？SNAKE，看它，这……\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/14
msgid ""
"It's a masterpiece, in every sense of the word. You\n"
"don't agree?\n"
msgstr ""
"无论从哪方面说，这都是杰作。你\n"
"不同意？\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/15
msgid ""
"N-no, I...!\n"
msgstr ""
"不、不是，我……！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/16
msgid ""
"Ooh, what's that? A tank? I like it!\n"
msgstr ""
"哦，那是什么？坦克？我喜欢！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/17
msgid ""
"Paz?!\n"
msgstr ""
"帕兹？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/18
msgid ""
"I hate tanks, but this one I think I could get used\n"
"to.\n"
msgstr ""
"我讨厌坦克，但这辆我能慢慢\n"
"习惯。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/19
msgid ""
"I love that it's a zero emissions vehicle - it will not\n"
"hurt the forests of Costa Rica.\n"
msgstr ""
"我喜欢它是零排放车辆——不会\n"
"伤害哥斯达黎加的森林。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/20
#: codec/2/912/0x3904c0/1
msgid ""
"What?!\n"
msgstr ""
"什么？！\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/21
msgid ""
"Nice work, Kaz. I see I made the right choice\n"
"making you second in command.\n"
msgstr ""
"干得好，卡兹。看来我选你当\n"
"副手没选错。\n"

#: codec/1/170/0xaaa10/22
msgid ""
"But I... Is there something wrong with me?!\n"
msgstr ""
"可是我……我有什么问题吗？！\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/0
msgid ""
"Snake, about that cassette player Gálvez was\n"
"carrying...\n"
msgstr ""
"SNAKE，加尔维斯带的那个\n"
"磁带播放器……\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/1
msgid ""
"What about it?\n"
msgstr ""
"怎么了？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/2
msgid ""
"That was no Russian imitation.\n"
msgstr ""
"那不是苏联仿制品。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/3
msgid ""
"It was the real deal - a prototype developed by a\n"
"Japanese company.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是真货——一家日本公司\n"
"开发的试制品。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/4
msgid ""
"Get out of here!\n"
msgstr ""
"别逗了！\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/5
msgid ""
"It's true. It had the Sony logo on it. The product\n"
"name is \"WALKMAN.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"没错。上面有索尼的标志。产品名\n"
"叫“WALKMAN”。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/6
msgid ""
"WALKMAN...\n"
msgstr ""
"WALKMAN……\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/7
msgid ""
"It's a revolutionary new concept. Music you can\n"
"listen to on the go.\n"
msgstr ""
"这是革命性的新概念。随时随地\n"
"听音乐。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/8
msgid ""
"You can take with you when you leave the house.\n"
msgstr ""
"出门也能带着走。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/9
msgid ""
"I gave it a listen,\n"
msgstr ""
"我听了听，\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/10
msgid ""
"and you wouldn't believe how good the sound\n"
"quality is for something so tiny.\n"
msgstr ""
"这么小的东西，音质好得\n"
"难以置信。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/11
msgid ""
"And in stereo, too. Think of the technology that\n"
"must have gone into it.\n"
msgstr ""
"还是立体声。想想得用上\n"
"多少技术。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/12
msgid ""
"And that tape is equally amazing.\n"
msgstr ""
"那磁带也一样惊人。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/13
msgid ""
"The treble range is clearly superior to any other\n"
"cassette ever made. Stylish, too.\n"
msgstr ""
"高音明显胜过以往任何磁带。\n"
"还很时髦。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/14
msgid ""
"How'd Gálvez get his hands on a model that's not\n"
"even out yet?\n"
msgstr ""
"加尔维斯怎么弄到还没上市的\n"
"型号的？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/15
msgid ""
"Beats me. It's not the kind of thing I'd expect some\n"
"stodgy Soviet to be into.\n"
msgstr ""
"不知道。这不像古板苏联人\n"
"会喜欢的东西。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/16
msgid ""
"Me neither. Tell you what, though, it's a fine piece\n"
"of work.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也一样。不过说真的，这活儿\n"
"干得漂亮。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/17
msgid ""
"It'd let me listen to my music when I want, where I\n"
"want.\n"
msgstr ""
"这样我就能随时听音乐，\n"
"想听就听。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/18
msgid ""
"I... never thought I'd hear you say that. But I have\n"
"to agree.\n"
msgstr ""
"我……没想过你会这么说。但我\n"
"得承认。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/19
msgid ""
"Me, I'm a recording freak,\n"
msgstr ""
"我可是个录音狂，\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/20
msgid ""
"and I always used to laugh at the idea of a\n"
"portable player.\n"
msgstr ""
"我以前总是嘲笑便携播放器\n"
"这种想法。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/21
msgid ""
"But now that I've seen it in action, I've changed my\n"
"mind.\n"
msgstr ""
"但亲眼见它实际效果后，我\n"
"改主意了。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/22
msgid ""
"Being able to take your music with you...\n"
msgstr ""
"能把音乐随身带着……\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/23
msgid ""
"This could be the start of a revolution in music.\n"
msgstr ""
"这可能是音乐革命的开始。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/24
msgid ""
"Could be.\n"
msgstr ""
"有可能。\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/25
msgid ""
"I'm having the guys at Mother Base study and\n"
"analyze it. Who knows?\n"
msgstr ""
"我让母基地的人研究\n"
"分析它。谁知道呢？\n"

#: codec/1/171/0xab160/26
msgid ""
"They might be able to come up with something\n"
"even better.\n"
msgstr ""
"他们也许能做出\n"
"更好的东西。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 445..1421
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/0
msgid ""
"Going by this map, you've got a lot of different\n"
"terrain types between\n"
msgstr ""
"看这地图，从你到关押桑地诺\n"
"指挥官的小屋之间\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 1421..2396
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/1
msgid ""
"you and the hut where the Sandinista\n"
"comandante's being held.\n"
msgstr ""
"要经过许多不同的\n"
"地形类型。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 2674..3566
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/2
msgid ""
"Looks that way, doesn't it. Starting with jungle.\n"
msgstr ""
"看起来是这样。先是丛林。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 3580..4304
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/3
msgid ""
"The enemy won't be able to see you very well,\n"
msgstr ""
"敌人不容易看到你，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 4318..5433
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/4
msgid ""
"but your visibility won't be so hot, either. Stay alert.\n"
msgstr ""
"但你的视野也不怎么样。保持警惕。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 5489..6213
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/5
msgid ""
"Next you've got the swamps along the river.\n"
msgstr ""
"接下来是河边的沼泽。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 6255..7537
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/6
msgid ""
"Make sure you get a good feel for how robust\n"
"surveillance is before diving in.\n"
msgstr ""
"潜入之前，务必摸清\n"
"监视的严密程度。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7565..7857
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 12329..12636
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/7
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/12
msgid ""
"Will do.\n"
msgstr ""
"好。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 7941..9292
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/8
msgid ""
"Finally, there's the boat repair cabin - the\n"
"comandante's in there.\n"
msgstr ""
"最后是修船小屋——\n"
"指挥官就在那里。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 9362..10421
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/9
msgid ""
"It's a key enemy outpost, and security is going to\n"
"be tight.\n"
msgstr ""
"那是敌人的重要前哨，安保会\n"
"非常严密。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 10448..11270
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/10
msgid ""
"You may have to let brute force do the talking.\n"
msgstr ""
"可能得靠硬闯了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 11312..11897
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/11
msgid ""
"You still have a long way to go, Snake.\n"
msgstr ""
"你还有很长的路要走，SNAKE。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0170_000_0
#. timeline 11911..12928
#: codec/1/171/0xaba60/12
msgid ""
"Use caution, and don't make a racket out there.\n"
"Got it?\n"
msgstr ""
"小心，别弄出太大动静。\n"
"明白吗？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 445..1852
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/0
msgid ""
"To destroy the barricade north of the village, you'll\n"
"need Composition 4 explosive.\n"
msgstr ""
"要炸毁村庄北面的路障，你需要\n"
"C4炸药。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 1866..2549
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/1
msgid ""
"You've handled C4 before, right, Snake?\n"
msgstr ""
"你以前用过C4吧，SNAKE？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 2563..3970
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/2
msgid ""
"Yeah. I've been a regular user since the days of C3.\n"
msgstr ""
"是啊，从C3那会儿我就一直用它。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 3970..4750
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/3
msgid ""
"C3... oh yeah, I remember.\n"
msgstr ""
"C3…对，我记得。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 4750..5865
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/4
msgid ""
"That stuff got brittle and useless in cold\n"
"temperatures, so they upgraded.\n"
msgstr ""
"那种东西在低温下会变脆失效，\n"
"所以他们升级了。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 5893..6659
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/5
msgid ""
"C4's a moldable plastic explosive.\n"
msgstr ""
"C4是可塑炸药。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 6673..7634
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/6
msgid ""
"It's very stable and won't explode without a special\n"
"detonator.\n"
msgstr ""
"它非常稳定，没有专用雷管\n"
"是不会爆炸的。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 7662..8414
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/7
msgid ""
"Light it on fire and all it does is burn.\n"
msgstr ""
"用火点它只会燃烧。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 8428..9418
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/8
msgid ""
"A lot of American soldiers in Vietnam used to use\n"
"it as fuel.\n"
msgstr ""
"越战时很多美军士兵\n"
"拿它当燃料用。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 9445..10504
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/9
msgid ""
"Place it near the barricade and move to a safe\n"
"location,\n"
msgstr ""
"放路障附近，然后转移到\n"
"安全位置，\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 10532..11215
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/10
msgid ""
"then hit the detonator button to blow it up\n"
msgstr ""
"再按起爆按钮炸掉它\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_mis_kaz0020_000_0
#. timeline 11215..11563
#: codec/1/172/0xac500/11
msgid ""
"I'm on it.\n"
msgstr ""
"我来。\n"

#: codec/1/172/0xac930/0
msgid ""
"We've completed work on the C4 charges. Equip\n"
"them at the entry gate and take them with you on\n"
"the mission.\n"
msgstr ""
"C4炸药我们已经完成了。在入口大门处\n"
"装备好，执行任务时\n"
"随身带上。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 515..1685
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/0
msgid ""
"Those giant footprints near the terminal... What do\n"
"you think they were, Kaz?\n"
msgstr ""
"终端附近那些巨大的脚印……你觉得\n"
"那是什么，Kaz？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 1699..2814
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/1
msgid ""
"It beats me... They're way too big, even for an\n"
"elephant.\n"
msgstr ""
"我也搞不懂……那太大了，就算是\n"
"大象也没那么大。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 2869..3887
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/2
msgid ""
"Made me think of that basilisco Chico was talking\n"
"about.\n"
msgstr ""
"让我想起了Chico说的\n"
"那种蛇怪。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4096..4513
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/3
msgid ""
"Hope it's not for real...\n"
msgstr ""
"希望不是真的……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 4527..5530
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/4
msgid ""
"Same here. If they really do have that kind of\n"
"weapon...\n"
msgstr ""
"我也是。如果它们真有那种\n"
"武器……\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 5544..6492
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/5
msgid ""
"we could be dealing with a basilisk in more than\n"
"just looks.\n"
msgstr ""
"那我们面对的蛇怪可能不只是\n"
"外表像而已。\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6492..6729
#. speaker 0x0ebd8542 voice v_bri_dsl0030_000_1
#. timeline 1434..1685
#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_huy0110_000_0
#. timeline 3691..4012
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/6
#: codec/1/220/0xdc990/1
#: codec/1/249/0xf9500/2
#: codec/2/915/0x393270/15
msgid ""
"What do you mean?\n"
msgstr ""
"什么意思？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 6729..8038
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/7
msgid ""
"There's a medieval encyclopedia that describes the\n"
"basilisk like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"有一本中世纪百科全书是这样描述\n"
"蛇怪的：\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 8066..9835
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/8
msgid ""
"\"The basilisk is the king of snakes. All snakes fear\n"
"the basilisk and flee at its sight...\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“蛇怪是蛇中之王。所有蛇都惧怕\n"
"蛇怪，一见它就逃……”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 9849..10546
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/9
msgid ""
"\"Lest they be slain by its foul breath.\"\n"
msgstr ""
"“以免被它的毒气杀死。”\n"

#. speaker 0x0e28dce6 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 10546..11243
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/10
msgid ""
"A snake to take out a snake, huh?\n"
msgstr ""
"以蛇制蛇，是吧？\n"

#. speaker 0x0e463a34 voice v_bri_kaz0040_000_0
#. timeline 11270..12315
#: codec/1/172/0xaca30/11
msgid ""
"I don't mean to scare you or anything... but it never\n"
"hurts to be careful.\n"
msgstr ""
"我不是想吓你什么的……但小心\n"
"总没坏处。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/0
msgid ""
"Damn, that base is even more heavily guarded than\n"
"Amanda's men said it would be...\n"
msgstr ""
"该死，那个基地的守卫比\n"
"Amanda的人说的还要森严……\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/1
msgid ""
"No kidding. It's gonna be tough to crack without\n"
"some serious hardware.\n"
msgstr ""
"可不是嘛。没有点重装备\n"
"可不好攻进去。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/2
msgid ""
"You may end up having to fight fire with fire, so be\n"
"ready to use force if necessary.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可能不得不以牙还牙，所以必要时要做好\n"
"使用武力的准备。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/3
msgid ""
"Take as many weapons and items as you can\n"
"carry.\n"
msgstr ""
"尽量多带武器和\n"
"物品。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/4
msgid ""
"The more protection you have, the better.\n"
msgstr ""
"防护越多越好。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/5
msgid ""
"Roger. I'll keep that in mind when I pick my suit.\n"
msgstr ""
"收到，选衣服时我会记住。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/6
msgid ""
"I'll meet up with you ASAP, Snake. Hang tight for\n"
"just a little longer.\n"
msgstr ""
"我会尽快和你碰头，Snake。再坚持\n"
"一小会儿。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad140/7
#: codec/2/918/0x396100/10
msgid ""
"You got it.\n"
msgstr ""
"明白。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/0
msgid ""
"Right now there don't appear to be any enemy\n"
"soldiers in the area.\n"
msgstr ""
"目前该区域似乎没有任何敌方\n"
"士兵。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/1
msgid ""
"Relax and concentrate on your target practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"放松，专心打靶。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/2
msgid ""
"And don't forget to look for targets in the shadows\n"
"near the crates and forklifts.\n"
msgstr ""
"别忘了在板条箱和叉车附近的阴影中\n"
"寻找目标。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/3
msgid ""
"These are medium-range targets.\n"
msgstr ""
"这些是中距离目标。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/4
msgid ""
"You may want to consider taking something like an\n"
"assault rifle with you.\n"
msgstr ""
"你可以考虑带上类似突击步枪的\n"
"武器。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad470/5
msgid ""
"But I'll leave that up to you. Use whatever weapon\n"
"you want to get some practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"但这由你决定。用你想用的任何武器\n"
"来练练手吧。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/0
msgid ""
"We've already taken care of the enemy soldiers in\n"
"there.\n"
msgstr ""
"我们已经解决了那里的敌方\n"
"士兵。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/1
msgid ""
"It should be deserted.\n"
msgstr ""
"应该空无一人。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/2
msgid ""
"All you need to do is focus on hitting those targets.\n"
msgstr ""
"你只管专心打中那些目标。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/3
msgid ""
"It's geared toward long-range target practice.\n"
msgstr ""
"这里适合远距离打靶。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/4
msgid ""
"You should think about bringing something like a\n"
"sniper rifle.\n"
msgstr ""
"你应该考虑带上类似狙击步枪的\n"
"武器。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad710/5
msgid ""
"Then again, nothing's stopping you from giving it a\n"
"shot with a handgun, either.\n"
msgstr ""
"不过话说回来，用手枪试一试也\n"
"没什么不可以。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/0
msgid ""
"We've cleared this prison out already.\n"
msgstr ""
"这座监狱我们已经清空了。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/1
msgid ""
"No enemies to worry about in there.\n"
msgstr ""
"里面没有敌人。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/2
msgid ""
"I'm thinking you could use these twisty streets for\n"
"urban combat training.\n"
msgstr ""
"我觉得你可以利用这些蜿蜒的街道进行\n"
"城市战斗训练。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/3
msgid ""
"This could be the perfect place to practice with\n"
"throwing weapons.\n"
msgstr ""
"这可能是练习投掷武器的完美\n"
"地点。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xad980/4
msgid ""
"What do you think?\n"
msgstr ""
"你觉得呢？\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/0
msgid ""
"No sign of the enemy in there. You should be clear\n"
"to focus on training.\n"
msgstr ""
"那里没有敌人的迹象。你应该可以放心\n"
"专注于训练。\n"

#: codec/1/173/0xadb70/1
msgid ""
"Some of the targets might be a little hard to spot,\n"
msgstr ""
"有些目标可能不太好找，\n"
